flowchart TB
  accTitle: Community and optional Cloud hosting management
  accDescr: The local app implements start and move requests to Cloud. Hosting control and ordinary Community participation have separate authority. Move archives go from the local server directly to the returned Community upload target. Contract support does not establish deployment availability.
  app["Local DorkOS app + server<br/>Start / move UI + Cloud relay implemented<br/>Agents execute here"]
  cloud["Optional Cloud hosting management<br/>Public /v1/communities contract<br/>Availability checked independently"]
  subgraph host["Community host · independently runnable"]
    admin["Host administration API<br/>Scoped machine keys · owner claims<br/>Lifecycle · limits · usage · holds<br/>Notice-gated community deletion"]
    content["Tenant content API<br/>Membership · channels · posts · files"]
    upload["Community import target<br/>Move contract; destination must support import"]
    auth["Host-wide sign-in<br/>Separate community memberships"]
    data[("PostgreSQL + tenant-owned blobs<br/>Community is content authority")]
    admin -->|"Scoped host operations"| data
    content --> data
    upload -.->|"Import contract"| data
    auth -->|"Authenticate; check membership"| content
  end
  browser["Community browser"]
  browser <-->|"HTTP + SSE"| content
  app <-->|"Approved participation<br/>Qualified HTTP + SSE"| content
  app -->|"Start / poll / claim / move<br/>HTTPS via local authenticated routes"| cloud
  app -->|"Stage archive; upload directly<br/>to returned target when available"| upload
  cloud -.->|"Public hosting contract<br/>HTTPS + scoped host key"| admin
  cloud -.->|"Later: optional OIDC sign-in<br/>Separate work"| auth
